1	// config-to-document — the page's edit mode ("Edit" button in the top bar).
2	//
3	// A consultant or key user corrects the consultant notes and the reference
4	// panel, the value tables (card title, cells, rows) and the change history in
5	// the finished document, with nothing installed and nothing loaded from the
6	// network. Edited views carry an "Edited" badge; their SM30 drawings are drawn
7	// again from the edited rows at the next build.
8	//   · click a text to change it (plain text); add or delete list items, add
9	//     notes to an activity that has none, delete a source
10	//   · replace a drawn SM30 screen with a real screenshot (button, or Ctrl+V on the
11	//     selected drawing) and back to the drawing
12	//   · undo every change (Ctrl+Z outside a text field, or the Undo button),
13	//     autosave to the browser (IndexedDB) with "continue editing" on reopen
14	//   · "Save" asks for author and change note and downloads the page again with
15	//     every edited note embedded (<script id="config-edits">);
16	//     `build-config-doc.mjs --import <file>` merges them into notes/edits.json,
17	//     so the next version keeps the edits.
18	//
19	// Edits replace the whole note of an activity and are system-specific: the
20	// knowledge base (notes.mjs kb) never takes them.
21	
